#
# Counter-example for the native math:UnrecordedProjectionLoss gate
# (crates/validate/src/lint.rs, check_math_unrecorded_projection_loss): a LOSSY
# math:ProjectionRecord (logic:preservationKind logic:SoundUnderApproximation) projects
# a math:MathematicalExpression source — a structured AST, not a bare display string —
# but its logic:unsupportedConstruct enumeration names an UNRELATED drop, never the
# expression's own structural flattening. Collapsing the AST to
# math:projectionTargetName's string-only external target is exactly the loss the
# ledger exists to record. The native gate MUST emit math:UnrecordedProjectionLoss (and
# NOT math:UndeclaredUnsupportedConstruct, since a construct IS enumerated — just not
# the flattened expression).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

# The projection SOURCE has to stay an asserted math:MathematicalExpression — that asserted
# typing is exactly what math:UnrecordedProjectionLoss triggers on ("a structured AST, not a
# bare display string"). It also names a concrete form, math:SymbolReference, because the
# abstract base alone names none and would raise math:UnrecognizedExpressionType beside the
# one class this fixture isolates.
ex:sumExpr a math:SymbolReference , math:MathematicalExpression ;
    math:hasMathematicalSymbol ex:sumExprSymbol .
ex:sumExprSymbol a math:MathematicalSymbol .

ex:exprProjection a math:ProjectionRecord ;
    math:projectionSource ex:sumExpr ;
    math:projectionTargetName "OWL annotation (string only)" ;
    logic:preservationKind logic:SoundUnderApproximation ;
    logic:unsupportedConstruct "irrelevant-other-drop" .
